# Highnoon Visitor Management System (VMS)

A robust, enterprise-grade Django application designed to streamline, track, and audit visitor traffic across multiple corporate facilities and branches. Built with Django, Bootstrap 5, Select2, and Chart.js, Highnoon VMS offers live check-in/check-out tracking, retroactive revision logging, dynamic role-based access control, and detailed analytics with downloadable PDF reports.

---

## Key Features

### Multi-Branch & Role-Based Access Control
- **Scoped Visibility** — Automatically filters visitor records based on the logged-in user's assigned company and branch (`sys_usr_system`).
- **Superuser Controls** — Superusers and elevated roles can toggle filters to audit data across all corporate branches and companies.

### Live Visit Management & Revisions
- **On-the-Spot Check-In/Out** — Issue active visitor cards, log visit purposes, and record exact check-in/check-out timestamps.
- **Backlogs & Revisions** — Log retroactive visits or update historical entries seamlessly using dynamic, single-series delegated modals across paginated data views.
- **Smart Visitor-Employee Auto-fill** — Remembers previous host employees for returning visitors to speed up registration.

### Analytics & Reporting Engine
- **Summary Reports** — Aggregate visit counts, distinct visitor counts, total duration, and visit time breakdown dynamically grouped by Purpose, Company, Branch, Department, Division, Employee, or Visitor.
- **History Reports** — Searchable historical logs with filters for date range (defaulting to the 1st of the current month through today), status, purpose, host employee (with designation), and visitor details.
- **Visual Dashboards** — Integrated Chart.js horizontal bar charts and entry traffic load metrics (excluded from exports to keep PDFs clean).
- **Exportable PDF Reports** — Single-click generation of formatted A4 portrait PDFs for both Summary and History reports.

---

## Tech Stack

| Layer | Technologies |
|---|---|
| **Backend** | Python 3.x, Django 4.x / 5.x |
| **Frontend** | HTML5, CSS3, JavaScript (ES6+), Bootstrap 5, jQuery |
| **UI Components** | Select2, Flatpickr (24h format), FontAwesome 6 |
| **Analytics & Visualization** | Chart.js |
| **PDF Generation** | xhtml2pdf / ReportLab |
| **Database** | PostgreSQL / MySQL / SQLite |

---

## Repository Structure

```text
├── masters/            # Master tables (Companies, Branches, Departments, Employees, Purposes)
├── visitors/            # Visitor profiles and Card assignment models
├── visits/               # Core Visit models, backlog workflows, and check-in/out views
├── reports/             # Summary & History aggregations, PDF export logic
├── templates/
│   ├── base.html        # Base layout template
│   ├── visits/           # Visit listing & revision backlog templates
│   └── reports/         # Summary/History HTML views & PDF layout templates
├── manage.py
└── requirements.txt
```

---

## Installation & Setup

### 1. Prerequisites
Ensure you have Python 3.10+ and pip installed on your machine.

### 2. Clone the Repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/your-username/highnoon-vms.git
cd highnoon-vms
```

### 3. Set Up Virtual Environment
```bash
# On Linux / macOS
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

# On Windows
python -m venv venv
venv\Scripts\activate
```

### 4. Install Dependencies
```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 5. Database Migrations
```bash
python manage.py makemigrations
python manage.py migrate
```

### 6. Create Superuser
```bash
python manage.py createsuperuser
```

### 7. Run Development Server
```bash
python manage.py runserver
```

Navigate to [http://127.0.0.1:8000/](http://127.0.0.1:8000/) in your browser.

---

## Permissions Configuration

To access specific sections of the platform, ensure users or groups are assigned the proper Django permissions:

| Permission | Grants Access To |
|---|---|
| `visits.view_visit` | Access live visit lists |
| `visits.add_visit` / `visits.change_visit` | Create new visits and process check-outs |
| `visits.can_view_backlogs` | Access Revisions / Backlogs management |
| `reports.view_reports` | View Summary and History analytics tabs |
| `reports.download_reports` | Download PDF summaries and history logs |

